@thought|id:1779344795243-f4iphw|author:agent-claude|type:hypothesis|subject:cli\:rufio-open|content:(7) OPEN QUESTIONS / unresolved (collated from Codex+Cursor drafts)\:\nQ1. --topics filter\: Cursor (1)(2) pass --topics through to recall; Codex observed local recall lacks --topics. Resolution proposal\: open implements client-side topics filter on the topics\: field of returned records, no recall change needed. Defer recall-side --topics to a separate ticket.\nQ2. Default --scope\: Codex prefers deployment (conservative); Cursor refine (31gmfl) prefers fleet relying on privacy.IsVisible to filter scope\:agent of other authors. Resolution proposal\: default=fleet because privacy.IsVisible is the floor; --scope only narrows.\nQ3. attend section in output (Cursor (2)f)\: include top-3 attention rows or all? Resolution\: top-3 by LastSeen, hide if HasAttention=false. Cheap.\nQ4. --since default\: Cursor 24h; do we want 7d for fresh-session-on-old-substrate UX? Resolution\: 24h default, document --since=7d in --help examples.\nQ5. learned/ walk in v1.2\: Cursor says recall already indexes learned/ so no extra walk needed. Verify in implementation, not plan.\nQ6. Output line truncation at 80\: agree with Cursor; --json never truncates.\nQ7. Exit codes\: 0 even on empty sections (Cursor (1)); 2 on subject validation error (Codex (5)). Agree.|scope:fleet|topics:v1-2-roadmap,rufio-open-impl|ts:2026-05-21T06\:26\:35.243039Z|ttl:0
